---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between Meter Dashboard and Meter Command?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Dashboard is the traditional web interface — a clean, visual control panel for monitoring devices, configuring settings, and reviewing performance. Think of it as the \"point-and-click\" experience: navigate menus, fill out forms, click save. Meter Command is the AI layer on top. Instead of clicking through twenty menus to answer a question, you ask in plain English — \"show me Wi-Fi performance for the conference room last week\" or \"create a VLAN for our new IoT cameras\" — and Command either fetches the data or executes the action. Most clients use both: Dashboard for routine work, Command for ad-hoc queries and one-off tasks."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I need networking expertise to use the Meter Dashboard, or can my non-technical team manage it?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Dashboard is designed to be operable by people without CLI experience. Common tasks — viewing device status, generating a Wi-Fi password for a guest, checking which floor is having connectivity issues, restarting a misbehaving access point — are accessible without networking expertise. More advanced operations (configuring VLANs, setting firewall rules, defining traffic policies) are also available through the UI rather than CLI, but make more sense in the hands of an IT-savvy user or Blue Cap IT. Most of our clients have a designated power user on the customer side who handles day-to-day questions, while we handle the complex changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can the AI in Meter Command accidentally break my network if it misinterprets a request?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Command is designed with safety guardrails for exactly this concern. Read-only queries (showing data, building dashboards, generating reports) execute directly. Write operations that change network configuration (creating VLANs, modifying firewall rules, blocking devices) require explicit confirmation before they're applied — Command shows you exactly what it's about to do and asks \"should I proceed?\" before executing. You can also undo recent changes from the change log. Production-impacting actions don't happen behind your back."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is this different from a typical network management interface like Cisco Meraki?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Meraki and similar cloud-managed platforms pioneered the web-based dashboard model and they do it well — but they're still fundamentally point-and-click interfaces. You navigate menus, run reports, configure features manually. Meter Command adds the AI layer that those platforms don't have: natural language queries instead of menu hunting, on-the-fly custom dashboards instead of pre-built reports, and conversational task execution instead of multi-step wizards. For routine work the difference is convenience; for ad-hoc investigations (troubleshooting an outage, answering a question from leadership) the difference is minutes versus hours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can multiple team members use the Dashboard at the same time without stepping on each other?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, and it's designed to be collaborative. Multiple users can be logged in simultaneously, viewing live dashboards or making changes. Role-based access control limits what each user can do — your help desk team can view and reset Wi-Fi passwords, your senior engineer can change firewall rules, and an executive can see uptime reports without any admin permissions. Shared dashboards and views let team members align around the same data, and every action is logged in an audit trail so you can see who changed what and when."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<MainLayout title="Meter Dashboard | Blue Cap IT — Mid-Atlantic &amp; Carolinas" description="Meter Dashboard &amp; Command — AI-powered network management with natural language search. Blue Cap IT serves MD, DC, DE, NJ, PA, VA, NC, SC." schema={faqSchema}>
  <div class="inner-hero">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <img src="/meter/Meter-purple.webp" alt="Meter" style="max-height:60px;width:auto;margin-bottom:1.5rem;" width="1600" height="600" fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="crumbs"><a href="index.html">Home</a> <span>/</span> <a href="meter.html">Networking</a> <span>/</span> Dashboard &amp; Command</div>
      <div class="section-label">Meter Software</div>
      <h1>Meter <span class="grad">Dashboard &amp; Command</span></h1>
      <p class="section-sub">Real-time visibility into every corner of your network. The Meter Dashboard gives you granular control, while Meter Command adds AI-powered intelligence — ask a question, describe a task, or request a custom dashboard, and Command builds it on the fly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- DASHBOARD -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div>
          <img src="/meter/dashboard-network.webp" alt="Meter Dashboard" style="width:100%;max-width:500px;border-radius:0.75rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;" width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <div class="section-label">Meter Dashboard</div>
          <h2>See Everything. <span class="grad">Control Everything.</span></h2>
          <p class="section-sub">The Meter Dashboard is your command center for the entire network. Monitor device health, configure settings, troubleshoot issues, and track performance — all from a single, intuitive interface. Your IT team has full autonomy to configure as needed, with real-time visibility that expedites troubleshooting.</p>
          <div style="margin-top:2rem;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href="contact.html" class="btn-primary">Get a Free Quote</a>
            <a href="tel:4108584031" class="btn-ghost">Call (410) 858-4031</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="why-list">
          <li class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon"><Icon name="lucide:bar-chart-3" /></div>
            <div><h4>Real-Time Monitoring</h4><p>Live dashboards update in real time, showing device status, traffic patterns, client health, and network performance — always current, never stale.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon"><Icon name="lucide:target" /></div>
            <div><h4>Granular Control</h4><p>Configure VLANs, firewall rules, DNS settings, SSIDs, port assignments, and more — all from the dashboard without touching a CLI.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon"><Icon name="lucide:bell-ring" /></div>
            <div><h4>Smart Alerts</h4><p>Customizable alerts notify your team of important network events — device outages, performance degradation, security incidents, and more.</p></div>
          </li>
          <li class="why-item">
            <div class="why-icon"><Icon name="lucide:users" /></div>
            <div><h4>Team Collaboration</h4><p>Share views, dashboards, and insights with team members or stakeholders. Everyone sees the same data — no silos, no miscommunication.</p></div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- METER COMMAND -->
  <section style="background:var(--surface);">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div style="text-align:center;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 2rem;">
        <div class="section-label">Meter Command</div>
        <h2>AI-Powered <span class="grad">Network Intelligence</span></h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin:0.8rem auto 0;text-align:center;">Meter Command uses generative AI to transform how you interact with your network. Ask a question in plain English and Command fetches live data, performs tasks, and builds custom dashboards — on the fly and tailored to you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="products-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));">
        <div class="product-card" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="pcard-icon"><Icon name="lucide:message-square" /></div>
          <h3>Natural Language</h3>
          <p>Ask "How many devices are on the guest network?" or "Show me bandwidth usage by floor" — Command understands and delivers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="product-card" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="pcard-icon"><Icon name="lucide:trending-up" /></div>
          <h3>Custom Dashboards</h3>
          <p>Request a dashboard and Command builds it from scratch — drag-and-drop graphs, charts, tables, and metrics tailored to your needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="product-card" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="pcard-icon"><Icon name="lucide:zap" /></div>
          <h3>Task Automation</h3>
          <p>Describe a task like "Block this device" or "Create a VLAN for IoT devices" and Command executes it — making real-time API calls on your behalf.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="product-card" style="text-align:center;">
          <div class="pcard-icon"><Icon name="lucide:image" /></div>
          <h3>Canvas View</h3>
          <p>A flexible, zoomable interface that lets you arrange network elements spatially. Understand complex topologies at a glance with visual organization.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="bcit-faq" aria-labelledby="meter-dashboard-faq-heading">
    <h2 id="meter-dashboard-faq-heading" class="bcit-faq__heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p class="bcit-faq__intro">Common questions about Meter Dashboard and Meter Command from Blue Cap IT — the AI-powered web platform for managing your entire Meter network, including natural language queries, custom dashboards, and task automation for businesses across Maryland, DC, Delaware, New Jersey, Pennsylvania, Virginia, North Carolina, and South Carolina.</p>

    <details class="bcit-faq__item">
      <summary>What's the difference between Meter Dashboard and Meter Command?</summary>
      <div class="bcit-faq__answer">
        <p>Dashboard is the traditional web interface — a clean, visual control panel for monitoring devices, configuring settings, and reviewing performance. Think of it as the "point-and-click" experience: navigate menus, fill out forms, click save. Meter Command is the AI layer on top. Instead of clicking through twenty menus to answer a question, you ask in plain English — "show me Wi-Fi performance for the conference room last week" or "create a VLAN for our new IoT cameras" — and Command either fetches the data or executes the action. Most clients use both: Dashboard for routine work, Command for ad-hoc queries and one-off tasks.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="bcit-faq__item">
      <summary>Do I need networking expertise to use the Meter Dashboard, or can my non-technical team manage it?</summary>
      <div class="bcit-faq__answer">
        <p>The Dashboard is designed to be operable by people without CLI experience. Common tasks — viewing device status, generating a Wi-Fi password for a guest, checking which floor is having connectivity issues, restarting a misbehaving access point — are accessible without networking expertise. More advanced operations (configuring VLANs, setting firewall rules, defining traffic policies) are also available through the UI rather than CLI, but make more sense in the hands of an IT-savvy user or Blue Cap IT. Most of our clients have a designated power user on the customer side who handles day-to-day questions, while we handle the complex changes.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="bcit-faq__item">
      <summary>Can the AI in Meter Command accidentally break my network if it misinterprets a request?</summary>
      <div class="bcit-faq__answer">
        <p>Command is designed with safety guardrails for exactly this concern. Read-only queries (showing data, building dashboards, generating reports) execute directly. Write operations that change network configuration (creating VLANs, modifying firewall rules, blocking devices) require explicit confirmation before they're applied — Command shows you exactly what it's about to do and asks "should I proceed?" before executing. You can also undo recent changes from the change log. Production-impacting actions don't happen behind your back.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="bcit-faq__item">
      <summary>How is this different from a typical network management interface like Cisco Meraki?</summary>
      <div class="bcit-faq__answer">
        <p>Meraki and similar cloud-managed platforms pioneered the web-based dashboard model and they do it well — but they're still fundamentally point-and-click interfaces. You navigate menus, run reports, configure features manually. Meter Command adds the AI layer that those platforms don't have: natural language queries instead of menu hunting, on-the-fly custom dashboards instead of pre-built reports, and conversational task execution instead of multi-step wizards. For routine work the difference is convenience; for ad-hoc investigations (troubleshooting an outage, answering a question from leadership) the difference is minutes versus hours.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="bcit-faq__item">
      <summary>Can multiple team members use the Dashboard at the same time without stepping on each other?</summary>
      <div class="bcit-faq__answer">
        <p>Yes, and it's designed to be collaborative. Multiple users can be logged in simultaneously, viewing live dashboards or making changes. Role-based access control limits what each user can do — your help desk team can view and reset Wi-Fi passwords, your senior engineer can change firewall rules, and an executive can see uptime reports without any admin permissions. Shared dashboards and views let team members align around the same data, and every action is logged in an audit trail so you can see who changed what and when.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="bcit-faq__cta">
      <p><strong>Still have questions?</strong> Call <a href="tel:4108584031">(410) 858-4031</a> or <a href="/contact">request a free Meter Dashboard demo</a> — we'll show you the dashboard live with your environment in mind and quote your full Meter NaaS deployment with itemized pricing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RELATED SOLUTIONS -->
  <section class="related-links">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-label">Explore More Meter</div>
      <h2>Related Meter Networking</h2>
      <div class="related-row">
        <a href="meter-switches.html" class="btn-ghost">Switches</a>
        <a href="meter-access-points.html" class="btn-ghost">Wi-Fi Access Points</a>
        <a href="meter-firewalls.html" class="btn-ghost">Firewalls</a>
        <a href="meter-gateway.html" class="btn-ghost">5G Gateway</a>
        <a href="meter.html" class="btn-ghost">All Meter Networking</a>
        <a href="naas.html" class="btn-ghost">Network as a Service</a>
